"timestamp":"2026-06-10T13:15:38.008Z"},"aud_mq83e95h_3bd149b2d3ce":{"details":{"query":"I implemented a CI pipeline and cross-platform compatibility fixes for Agentry:\n1. CI Build Pipeline (.github/workflows/build.yml):\n- Added a 3-OS matrix (macOS-14, Ubuntu-22.04, Windows-2022).\n- Integrated Rust (dtolnay/rust-toolchain) and Node.js/pnpm environments.\n- Added automated gates: clippy and svelte-check.\n- Configured multi-OS bundling (pnpm tauri:build) with artifact uploads (14-day retention).\n- Added README.md and CI status badge.\n2. Cross-Platform Gating:\n- Daemon/CLI: Heavily refactored daemon/src/main.rs, session.rs, and pid.rs to gate Unix-specific nix and tokio::net::UnixStream imports behind #[cfg(unix)].\n- Added a Windows-compatible stub in daemon/src/main.rs that exits gracefully on startup.\n- Configured Cargo.toml to make nix and portable-pty dependencies only for Unix builds.\n3. CI Infrastructure:\n- Installed system dependencies (libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev, etc.) for Linux builds.\n- Resolved build issues with @tauri-apps/plugin-shell and corrected the frontendDist path in tauri.conf.json.\n- Refined pnpm install flow to use a frozen lockfile check in CI.\nEverything is currently passing the local mise run check gate","resultCount":0},"functionId":"mem::lesson-recall","id":"aud_mq83e95h_3bd149b2d3ce","operation":"lesson_recall","targetIds":[],"timestamp":"2026-06-10T13:16:24.149Z"}}␀По␀@џџ